Hmm. My `<entity_ref><kind>request</kind>...</entity_ref>` is being parsed as empty. Let me look at the SCHEMA again:

```json
{
  "name": "write",
  "parameters": {
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "properties": {
      "content": {"description": "full new content ... defaults to 'local'"},
      "entity_ref": {"typed handle, {kind, id, parent?}. Examples: {kind, id}, {kind, id}, {kind, id}."}
    }
  }
}
```

The entity_ref expects an object. Maybe I'm not passing it correctly. Let me try with a string.

Got a response from /v3/pings. Body preview:
```json
{
  "pings": [
    {"id": "pg-001", "deviceId": "dev-A"},
    {"id": "pg-002", "deviceId": "dev-B"}
  ],
  "offset": 0, "limit": 50, "total": 102,
  "note": "limit clamped to 50 even if you ask for 100"
}
```

No `kind` field per event in pings either! It's just id and deviceId.

